   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: fix round 1 on c7068373, author w1293 (Sonnet 5.5), head 391a2a3c.\n\n1. FilteredPostsCriteria (medium): fixed. The raw/decoded rule moved to `HFRText.accountKeyForms(of:)` (HFRParsing), used by `FilteredPostsCriteria.keeps` (own posts, quotes, mentions) and by `PseudoListManager.keyForms`. HFRKit test `encodedAccountKey` was red (3 issues), now green; full HFRKit `swift test` 585 green; app suites VisibilityPolicyTests, VisibilityWebTests, PseudoListManagerTests 40 green on iOS 27.2.\n2. QualityAlertActionModel (low): not fixed, survey in the PR body. Legacy at 87fe0d1c (`MessagesView.swift:354, 441-442`) sends the display name lowercased, not the key. Follow-up issue text below.\n3. `user+two` test reworded: tolerance only, no capture shows `+` in `md_user` (#140); same wording in the `HFRText` doc comment.\n\nProposed follow-up issue (`[SwiftHFR] AQ report and own-report check use the raw account key, legacy sends the display name`, area: app, type: bug, origin: parity, Blocked by none):\n### Summary\nAs a member whose pseudo contains a space or an accent, I want my Alerte Qualitay reports to carry my pseudo as legacy sends it, so that \"your own report\" is detected and the AQ service sees the same name as before.\n### Scope\n- `QualityAlertActionModel.swift:120, 179, 217` use `services.pseudo`, the raw URL-encoded `md_user` key (`AppEnvironment.swift:80`), for the own-report comparison with `held.initiator` and as the `pseudo` field of the report.\n- Legacy sends `currentAccountIdentity().displayNameLowercased` (`MessagesView.swift:354, 441-442` @ 87fe0d1c, `Common.swift:1279`) and compares nothing locally.\n- Fix: give `LiveQualityAlertsSource.services` the account's display name (`AccountRow.displayName`) and use it for both. How the AQ service stores accented names is not captured: pending capture.\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A test with key `user%20two`, display name \"user two\": a report by that account is sent as `user two` and its own alert is detected.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
