   "body": "**mac/mac-mbp**: adversarial review round 2, reviewer r1300 (Opus 5.5), author w1293 (Sonnet 5.5).\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, r1300, head 391a2a3c)**\n\n**APPROVE**\n\nRound 1 re-checked:\n- Finding 1, fixed as a class. `HFRText.accountKeyForms(of:)` (`HFRParsing/Core/HFRText.swift:28`) is pure, Foundation-only and imports nothing new (ARCHITECTURE rules 2 and 5). `FilteredPostsCriteria.keeps` uses it for own posts, quotes and mentions. `PseudoListManager.keyForms` delegates to it with the same code, moved. The new API is an addition to HFRParsing, not an `HFRModels` type.\n- Finding 2. The legacy claim is checked: `MessagesView.swift:354` and `:441-442` at `87fe0d1c` send `currentAccountIdentity()?.displayNameLowercased`.\n- Finding 3, fixed: `+` is described as a tolerance only.\n\nFindings:\n1. **Low (process)**. The QualityAlert follow-up had to be an issue, not just a PR comment. The orchestrator has since filed it: #1302.\n2. **Detail**, `FilteredPostsCriteria.swift:53-54`. The raw form is also matched as a substring of the content HTML, so a link to `profilebdd.php?…&pseudo=user%20two` counts as a mention. This predates the PR, and the decoded form adds no false positive beyond legacy's display-name `contains`. Optional: match mentions on the decoded form only.\n\nVerified:\n- No other caller of `keyForms` or `accountKeyForms`.\n- Line lengths ≤ 140.\n- `kit-red.log` shows 3 failures before the fix, `kit-green.log` 585 HFRKit tests passing, and `fix1-summary.log` 40 app tests passing.\n- `swift test` not run: the Mac load was about 23.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
